      {
        "id": "sample_1",
        "type": "reg",
        "input": "3\n4\n6 6 6 6\n3\n5 1 4\n5\n2 1 2 1 1",
        "output": "0\n1\n2",
        "explanation": "Explanation:\nTest case 111: All the people already have an equal number of coins.\nTest case 222: The 2nd2^{nd}2nd person can become a monk and give his 111 coin to the person with 444 coins. After this, both the remaining people will have 555 coins.\nTest case 333: One way of two people becoming monks is as follows:\n\nThe 2nd2^{nd}2nd person becomes a monk, and takes his 111 coin with him\nThe 3rd3^{rd}3rd person becomes a monk, and gives one coin each to the 4th4^{th}4th and 5th5^{th}5th people\n\nEveryone remaining in the town now has 222 coins."
      }
    ]
